 -0.10; sign_p = one-sided sign test of anomaly < 0. Flag 'faster-melting roof (possible heat loss)' needs >= 4 observations, early_melt_share >= 0.6, median anomaly <= -0.10 and sign_p <= 0.1 (ties within 0.005 excluded). Apron = mapped driveway lines (only where block files hold them) buffered 1.5 m, compared with the median of open ground pixels (no roof).","limits":["A 20 m pixel is 400 m2; a typical house roof (100-250 m2) fills a quarter to a half of one pixel, so every roof value is mixed with yard, street, trees and neighbouring roofs ('mixed': true).","Neighbouring houses often share the same pixels, which pulls their values together and hides real differences.","Faster snow loss also comes from steep or south-facing pitches sliding/sun-melting, dark roofing, roof wind scour, shovelling, or trees/shadows in the pixel; heat loss is only one possible reason.","Driveways mapped as lines are ~3 m wide: far below one pixel. A clear driveway is most often shovelled or ploughed, not heated.","Snowfall is a station measurement up to tens of km away; local totals differ.","Few qualifying scenes per winter (clouds follow storms), so observation counts are small."],"summary":{"events":20,"events_with_scenes":8,"scenes_used":8,"houses":4,"flagged":0,"aprons":0,"median_roof_pixels":0.38}}